    "site_desc": "This site was established by Montana State University researchers in 2005 and re-instrumented in 2025 for above- and below-canopy eddy covariance. The tower is located in the Stringer Creek sub-watershed, which is maintained as an undisturbed lodgepole pine forest, and represents one of seven gaged sub-watersheds nested within the Tenderfoot Creek Experimental Forest. Historical data collection spanned the 2005-2012 (tall tower) and 2010-2012 (sub-canopy) time periods.",
